-- title:
--   Herbrand quotient of the fibre-grouped archimedean ideles
-- statement:
--   Let $K$ and $L$ be number fields with $L$ a Galois extension of $K$, and let $\sigma$ be a $K$-automorphism of $L$ such that every $K$-automorphism $\tau$ of $L$ lies in the subgroup of integer powers of $\sigma$ (so the Galois group is cyclic, generated by $\sigma$). Let $D$ be an ideles-Galois descent datum for $\mathcal O_L \subset L$ over $K$, i.e. a monoid homomorphism $D.\mathrm{act}$ from the group of $K$-automorphisms of $L$ to the ring automorphisms of the adele ring $\mathrm{AdeleRing}\,(\mathcal O_L)\,L$, compatible with the structure map from $L$ in the sense that $D.\mathrm{act}\,g$ sends the image of $x \in L$ to the image of $g(x)$, and acting continuously. Suppose given, for each infinite place $v$ of $K$, a multiplicative automorphism $\Phi a\, v$ of the unit group of $\prod_{w \mid v} L_w$, the product running over the infinite places $w$ of $L$ with $w \circ \mathrm{algebraMap}\,K\,L = v$, and assume the compatibility $h\Phi a$: for every such $v$, every unit $u$ of that fibre product and every infinite adele $x$ of $L$ whose coordinates at all $w \mid v$ are those of $u$, the infinite component of $D.\mathrm{act}\,\sigma\,(x,1)$ at each $w \mid v$ equals the corresponding coordinate of $\Phi a\,v\,u$. Let $d$ and $N$ be additive endomorphisms of the additivisation of $\prod_{v \mid \infty} (\prod_{w \mid v} L_w)^\times$ satisfying $d(u) = (v \mapsto \Phi a\,v\,(u\,v)) - u$ and $N(u) = \sum_{i < n} (v \mapsto (\Phi a\,v)^i (u\,v))$ additively, where $n$ is the cardinality of the group of $K$-automorphisms of $L$. Finally let $s_v$ be the number of infinite places of $L$ above $v$. Then the quotient of $\ker d$ by the image of $N$ has cardinality $\prod_{v \mid \infty} n / s_v$ (natural-number division), and the quotient of $\ker N$ by the image of $d$ has cardinality $1$.
--
--   This is the archimedean case of the computation of the Herbrand quotient of the idele group of a cyclic extension of number fields: the Tate cohomology groups $\hat H^0$ and $\hat H^{-1}$ of the archimedean part of the idele group, presented concretely as $\ker d/\mathrm{im}\,N$ and $\ker N/\mathrm{im}\,d$ for the difference and norm operators attached to the generator $\sigma$. The fibres over the places of $K$ are kept grouped here; the flat form over all infinite places of $L$ is derived from it in [`M4aHerbrand.infiniteIdele_tateCard_eq_localDegreeProd`](thm.html#M4aHerbrand.infiniteIdele_tateCard_eq_localDegreeProd).
